  ('fe961d55-3798-54b5-a795-fcb9a922cc8b', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', 'Which of the following is true about Madrid''s clean air zone? [A] Its effects are questionable它的治理效果尚存疑问。正反混淆 [B]It has been opposed by a judge正反混淆 [C] It needs tougher enforcement.无中生有 [D] Its fate is yet to be decided 阅读练习2 25 They should start by discarding California''s lame argument that exploring the contents of a smartphone— a vast storehouse of digital information—is similar to, say, going through a suspect''s purse. The court has ruled that police don''t violate the Fourth Amendment when they go through the wallet or pocketbook of an arrestee without a warrant. But exploring one''s smartphone is more like entering his or her home. A smartphone may contain an arrestee''s reading history, financial history, medical history and comprehensive records of recent correspondence. The development of "cloud computing," meanwhile, has made that exploration so much the easier. The author believes that exploring one’s phone contents is comparable to ______.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "getting into one’s residence闯入某人的住宅"}, {"key": "B", "text": "handling one’s historical records处理某人的历史档案"}, {"key": "C", "text": "scanning one’s correspondences翻阅 / 浏览某人的通信往来"}, {"key": "D", "text": "going through one’s wallet翻看、搜查某人的钱包"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '原文明确提到 "But exploring one''s smartphone is more like entering his or her home"（但探索一
个人的智能手机更像是进入他或她的家），直接对应选项 A 中的 "residence"（住所）。B 选项：handling
one’s historical records 处理某人各类历史记录原文只是举例：手机里包含阅读、财务、医疗记录，
这是手机储存的内容，不是作者拿来和 “搜查手机” 类比的对象。错误：混淆「手机里有什么内容」和
「搜查手机这件事类比成什么」，答非所问。C 选项：scanning one’s correspondences 浏览他人通讯记
录和 B 同理，correspondence（通讯记录）只是手机海量隐私信息里的其中一小部分，仅仅是手机包含
的内容，不是作者给出的类比参照物。错误：以局部细节冒充核心类比对象，偷换概念。选项 D1）加州
政府的观点：翻看手机内容 ≈ 搜查嫌疑人钱包（going through a suspect''s purse/wallet）', '英语2/长难句1-并列句【最终版】.pdf', 24, false, 104, null),
  ('3c33a8ed-3057-5293-9314-d9460e9c46f4', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', 'The author’s attitude to food self-sufficiency in the UK is____.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "defensive（防御，戒备）"}, {"key": "B", "text": "doubtful（怀疑的，不确定的）"}, {"key": "C", "text": "tolerant（宽容的）"}, {"key": "D", "text": "optimistic （乐观的) 30"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '', '英语2/长难句1-并列句【最终版】.pdf', 29, false, 112, null),
  ('e2d1e80c-39a6-5579-b683-ed05d0c70157', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', 'The key to mastering the art of deep work is to .', '[{"key": "A", "text": "keep to your focus time"}, {"key": "B", "text": "list your immediate tasks"}, {"key": "C", "text": "make specific daily plans"}, {"key": "D", "text": "seize every minute to work 阅读练习"}]'::jsonb, '', '', '英语2/长难句1-并列句【最终版】.pdf', 35, false, 121, null),
  ('463918b1-1094-5c72-b308-837a3fe27bed', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', 'The key to mastering the art of deep work is to .', '[{"key": "A", "text": "keep to your focus time"}, {"key": "B", "text": "list your immediate tasks列出你当下的任务"}, {"key": "C", "text": "make specific daily plans 制定详细的每日计划"}, {"key": "D", "text": "seize every minute to work抓紧每一分钟工作"}]'::jsonb, '', '', '英语2/长难句1-并列句【最终版】.pdf', 36, false, 122, null),
  ('0f58ec90-b3c8-5d57-9380-8b4d749f3c95', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', '句子组合 并列句：He is Jay and all teenagers admire him 套娃式复合句：He is who all teenagers admire. 连接词 6 连接词 基本意义 that 无实在意义 whether 是否 if 是否 who 谁 whom 谁 whose 谁的 what 什么 / 所……的事物，可指代物和人【没有选择范围】 I don''t know what kinds of books he likes. which 哪一个，可指代物和人【有选择范围的】 I don''t know which book he likes，the red one or the blue one when 指时间，什么时候 where 指地点，在哪里 why 指原因，为什么 how 指方式或程度，如何 名词性从句考法对比 7 初中题目 I believe ______ he will finish his homework on time.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "what"}, {"key": "B", "text": "that"}, {"key": "C", "text": "whose"}, {"key": "D", "text": "how 考研考法： The Supreme Court will now consider whether police can search the contents of a mobile phone without a warrant if the phone is on or around a person during an arrest."}]'::jsonb, '', '', '英语2/长难句2- 宾从.pdf', 5, false, 129, null),
  ('ef37624d-6ad0-53a1-9380-bc72b7ad86f2', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', '一般疑问句变宾语从句 主句: I’m not sure ______ 从句: Does my ginger cat still love me? 步骤一：入乡随俗 (调整语序，主语提前) my orange cat still loves me 步骤二：楚河分界 (加入连词) : if/whether 完整: I’m not sure if/whether my ginger cat still loves me. 怎么选择连接词？ 13 看看陈述句缺什么，缺人，连接词who，缺物，连接词what，缺是否，连接词if/whether，什么都不缺，填that 中文：我知道你昨天在商场买了一个苹果。 主句： I know 从句： you bought an apple in the shopping mall yesterday 例子1：从句什么都不缺： 宾语从句：I know (that) you bought an apple in the shopping mall yesterday 例子2：从句缺苹果（物）：2.you bought ____in the shopping mall yesterday 宾语从句：I know (what)you bought in the shopping mall yesterday 例子3：从句缺地点：2. you bought an apple_______ yesterday 宾语从句：I know (where) you bought an apple yesterday 例子4：从句缺时间：2. you bought an apple in the shopping mall 宾语从句：I know (when) you bought an apple in the shopping mall 例子5：从句缺是否: 2. 你昨天是否买了苹果 宾语从句：I don’t know（if /whether）you bought an apple in the shopping mall yesterday. 在宾语从句中，连词（连接词）不仅起到语法连接作用，还承载着特定的语义功能 考点一：宾语从句阅读方法 14 一.怎么判断句子的主句 步骤一：先把句子所有动词找出来 步骤二：找从句，从句=起点+从句谓语动词【途经】+终点。起点=连词 ；终点=下一个标点符号；下一 个连接词；下一个动词。 The Supreme Court will now consider whether police can search the contents of a mobile phone without a warrant if the phone is on or around a person during an arrest. 长难句阅读方法演示 步骤一：先把句子所有动词找出来 will consider；can search；is 步骤二：（起点）连词 whether；if 步骤二：（终点）下一个连词前 whether+can search+warrant 步骤二：（终点）下一个标点符号 if+is+arrest. 最高法院现在将审议在逮捕过程中，如果手机在被捕者身上或其周围，警 方是否可以在没有搜查令的情况下搜查手机内容 真题演练一 15 Just how much does the Constitution protect your digital data? The Supreme Court will now consider whether police can search the contents of a mobile phone without a warrant if the phone is on or around a person during an arrest. The Supreme Court will work out whether, during an arrest, it is legitimate to ______.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "prevent suspects from deleting their phone contents"}, {"key": "B", "text": "search for suspects'' mobile phones without a warrant"}, {"key": "C", "text": "check suspects'' phone contents without being authorized"}, {"key": "D", "text": "prohibit suspects from using their mobile phones"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '题目与原文对应关系：
原文明确提到最高法院将审议"whether police can search the contents of a mobile phone without a
warrant"（警方能否无搜查令搜查手机内容），这与选项C中的"check suspects'' phone contents without
being authorized"（未经授权查看嫌疑人手机内容）完全对应。
关键词匹配："search the contents" = "check...contents"（搜查/查看内容）"without a warrant" = "without
being authorized"（无搜查令/未经授权）。原文中的"warrant"特指法律程序中的"搜查令"，而"authorized"
是其同义替换。
排除其他选项：A项"阻止删除内容"：原文未提及数据删除问题。B项"无令搜查手机"：与原文接近，但
"search for phones"（搜查手机本身）与原文"search the contents"（搜查内容）范围不同。D项"禁止使用
手机"：与搜查内容无关。
长难句阅读法
18
DeSombre argues that the best way to collectively change the behavior of large
numbers of people is for the change to be structural.
第一步：找出所有动词
argues， to change，is ，to be
第二步：非谓语动词词组=起点+终点（前）
起点：to do/be；doing；done
终点=下一个标点符号前；下一个连接词前；
下一个动词前', '英语2/长难句2- 宾从.pdf', 12, false, 134, null),
  ('bf0b8326-832e-5c32-875f-6ad80eb2ffd7', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', 'According to the last paragraph, the real worry is ______.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "the vicious rivalry among big pharmas各大制药企业之间恶性竞争"}, {"key": "B", "text": "the ineffective enforcement of privacy law 隐私法实施不力"}, {"key": "C", "text": "the uncontrolled use of new software新软件不受管控的滥用"}, {"key": "D", "text": "the monopoly of big data by tech giants科技巨头对大数据的垄断 步骤①：上下文找复现词，快速了解文章背景，重点，预判大意"}]'::jsonb, '', '', '英语2/长难句3-主表同从.pdf', 27, false, 176, null),
  ('85d90329-de00-506e-b85a-56e6c823f062', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', 'that gives the data value. 强调句补充二; 结论：强调部分一般会成为考点 36 But this distinction misses the point that it is processing and aggregation, not the mere possession of bits, that gives the data value. 作用：通过调整句子结构或使用特定词汇，突出句子中的某个部分，使其更引人注意。 用 It is/was + 强调部分 + that/who + 句子剩余部分 特点：强调主语、宾语、状语等成分（不能强调谓语动词）。人用 who/that，物/时间/地点等用 that。 例子：原句：Tom broke the vase yesterday.（汤姆昨天打碎了花瓶。） 强调主语：It was Tom who/that broke the vase yesterday.（是汤姆昨天打碎了花瓶。） 强调宾语：It was the vase that Tom broke yesterday.（汤姆昨天打碎的是花瓶。） 强调时间：It was yesterday that Tom broke the vase.（是昨天汤姆打碎了花瓶。） 如何判断是强调结构：去掉强调结构，不影响句子完整性 not the mere possession of bits（插入语用作对比） 真题演练一 37 DeepMind has almost apologised. The NHS trust has mended its ways. Further arrangements—and there may be many—between the NHS and DeepMind will be carefully scrutinised to ensure that all necessary permissions have been asked of patients and all unnecessary data has been cleaned. There are lessons about informed patient consent to learn. But privacy is not the only angle in this case and not even the most important. Ms Denham chose to concentrate the blame on the NHS trust, since under existing law it "controlled" the data and DeepMind merely "processed" it. But this distinction misses the point that it is processing and aggregation, not the mere possession of bits, that gives the data value. The author argues in Paragraph 2 that ______.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "privacy protection must be secured at all costs必须不惜一切代价保护隐私"}, {"key": "B", "text": "leaking patients'' data is worse than selling it泄露患者数据比售卖患者数据性质更恶劣"}, {"key": "C", "text": "making profits from patients'' data is illegal利用患者数据牟利属于违法行为"}, {"key": "D", "text": "the value of data comes from the processing of it数据的价值来源于对数据的加工处理 C为什么不选:C. making profits from patients'' data is illegal利用 患者数据牟利属于违法行为"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '', '英语2/长难句3-主表同从.pdf', 35, false, 182, null),
  ('1cb87f25-4cd4-5c52-93ee-5861d0ebff7d', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', '：ACD 错在哪里 定位关键句："first-generation students may be most lacking not in potential but in practical knowledge about how to deal with the issues that face most college students" ❌ [A] may lack opportunities to apply for research projects 错因：无中生有 + 偷换概念 原文说的是缺乏 practical knowledge about how to deal with issues（处理问题的实践知识） A 选项把它偷换成了 opportunities to apply for research projects（申请研究项目的机会） research projects 这个概念在原文中根本不存在 出题人埋坑：利用"大学生"背景，诱导你联想到"科研项目"，但原文讨论的是"practical knowledge"（实践知识），而非 "opportunities"（机会）。 ❌ [C] can have a potential influence on other students 错因：曲解原文词汇 原文的 potential 是指"潜力、潜能"，用于说明第一代大学生不是没有潜力 C 选项把 potential 曲解成了"潜在的"（potential as an adjective），然后造出"对其他学生有潜在影响"这个意思 出题人埋坑：利用同一个词的不同词性和含义制造干扰，考生看到"potential"就以为对上了，实际上完全偏离原意。 [D] are actually indifferent to the achievement gap 错因：无中生有 + 相反方向原文说 "close the achievement gap"（缩小成绩差距），这是研究者想要达成的目标 第一代大学生是受害者/对象（他们的成绩差距需要被缩小），而不是对这个问题漠不关心的人 indifferent（漠不关心）这个态度在原文中完全没有依据 出题人埋坑：利用"achievement gap"这个原文词汇，但给它强加了"漠不关心"的负面态度，属于典型的"用原文词包装 错误意思"。 真题演练三 42 自然段一： ①Americans should take steps to protect their digital privacy. ②Despite the fact that keeping sensitive information on devices such as phones is increasingly a requirement of normal life，citizens still have a right to expect private documents to remain private and protected by the Constitution’s prohibition on unreasonable searches. In Paragraphs 1，the author shows his concern that ______.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "principles are hard to be clearly expressed各项准则难以清晰阐明"}, {"key": "B", "text": "the court is giving police less room for action法院留给警方的操作空间正在缩小"}, {"key": "C", "text": "citizens’ privacy is not effectively protected公民的隐私未能得到有效保护"}, {"key": "D", "text": "phones are used to store sensitive information手机被用来储存敏感信息"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '原文重点：作者提到，尽管在数字设备上存储敏感信息已成为现代生活的常态，但公民仍有权期望
私人文件受到保护，并受到宪法禁止不合理搜查的保障。这暗示当前公民的隐私可能未得到充分保护。
选项分析：A项“原则难以明确表达”未提及。B项“法院给警察的行动空间更小”与段落无关。C项“公民隐私
未得到有效保护”与作者担忧一致。D项“手机用于存储敏感信息”是事实陈述，但非作者主要关切。排除法：
D是现象描述，而C是作者的核心观点，因此选C。
