  ('b560691c-8660-5247-8723-b46ff69428c4', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', '', '[{"key": "A", "text": "after"}, {"key": "B", "text": "until"}, {"key": "C", "text": "while"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Since while A， B though/although A，B 考场攻略 19 The correlation between happiness and investment was particularly strong for younger firms,.... The relationship was 15 also stronger in places where happiness was spread more 16.equally.Firms seem to invest more in places where most people are relatively happy, rather than in places with happiness inequality. _17__ this doesn’t prove that happiness causes firms to invest more or to take a longer-term view, the authors believe it at least 18 hints at that possibility."}]'::jsonb, '', '', '英语2/长难句5预习版.pdf', 18, false, 191, null),
  ('658b0ba4-03b9-5f04-8697-39f1fdf0eee0', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', '', '[{"key": "A", "text": "after"}, {"key": "B", "text": "until"}, {"key": "C", "text": "while"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Since 对立点：主句强调现象的存在（相关性很强）。 从句强调现象的不确定性（无法证明因果关系）。 两者围绕同一话题（幸福与投资的关系） Recap 20 Thanks."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '', '英语2/长难句5预习版.pdf', 19, false, 192, null),
  ('0a2f1af6-058c-5dd0-898b-d3e7438d45e9', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', '_______ When you meet a person for the first time, make an effort to find the things which you and that person have in common so that you can build the conversation from that point. When you start conversation from there and then move outwards, you''ll find all of a sudden that the conversation becomes a lot easier.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Just say it"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Be present"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Pay a unique compliment"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Name, places, things"}, {"key": "E", "text": "Find the“me too\"s F.Skip the small talk"}]'::jsonb, 'E', '题目描述的是初次见面时，应努力寻找与对方的共同点（things which you and that person have in
common），并以此为基础展开对话。这种方法会使对话变得更轻松自然。E选项“Find the ''me too''s” 直接
对应“寻找共同点”这一策略，强调通过发现彼此的共同之处（如兴趣、经历等）来建立联系，与题目描述完
全契合。其他选项不符合题意：A（直接表达）未提及共同点；B（专注当下）与话题无关；C（独特赞美）
偏离核心；D（名字、地点、事物）过于宽泛；F（跳过寒暄）与建议的对话方式矛盾。因此，E为最佳答案。
